      "math_academy_id": "q-127269",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d8297713-fb86-59f2-af4d-850af2575541",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Non-Uniform Probability",
      "problem": "The absolute difference between the outcomes of one roll of two fair six-sided dice follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected value of the absolute difference of the outcomes for one roll of the two dice?\n\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{5}{18}$ | $\\frac{4}{18}$ | $\\frac{3}{18}$ | $\\frac{2}{18}$ | $\\frac{1}{18}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{6})+1(\\frac{5}{18})+2(\\frac{4}{18})+3(\\frac{3}{18})+4(\\frac{2}{18})+5(\\frac{1}{18}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{5}{18}+\\frac{8}{18}+\\frac{9}{18}+\\frac{8}{18}+\\frac{5}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+5+8+9+8+5}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
