      "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. For q-122412, total probability gives (0.014-0.01·0.80)/0.20=0.03. For q-89042, it gives (0.12-0.10·0.60)/0.40=0.15. For q-36915, the repeated club counts once, leaving five unique elements. For q-104909, each nested set counts as one element, giving five elements. Coefficient matrices record variable coefficients in the stated order, with zero for absent variables; augmented matrices append the constants. Thus q-129052 has rows (5,-8,1), (0,9,0), (3,-1,-8), and q-1050 has rows (1,3), (2,0). For q-1052, rearranging gives 2x-3y=5 and -4x+y=-6. For q-1051, the second equation has zero y coefficient. For q-129133 and q-129129, reading each matrix row as an equation gives the selected systems; terminal punctuation in the source does not change their meaning. For q-129137 and q-71734, the equations are already ordered for direct augmentation. For q-127375, the uniform mean is (21+30)/2=25.5. For q-126790, the mean is (0+1+2+3+4+5)/6=5/2. Its source contains the indexing typo 4·f(5) where 4·f(4) is expected; both probabilities equal 1/6, so the displayed expression and final answer remain numerically correct. For q-127269, the weighted sum is (5+8+9+8+5)/18=35/18. For q-127260, it is 3/8+2/4+3/8=5/4. No earlier submitted answers or revealed grades are provided; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions.",
